  "summary_en": "Florida's Unmanned Aircraft Systems Act (s. 330.41) vests drone regulation in the state, preempts local ordinances, protects drone delivery ports, and criminalises drone operation over critical infrastructure, schools, agricultural lands and private property, with federal FAA rules guiding construction.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "State preempts local regulation of drone design, operation, licensing and certification",
   "Localities cannot block drone delivery services based on drone port location",
   "Operating drones over critical infrastructure is a third-degree felony, with exceptions",
   "Drone operation over schools and agricultural lands is a misdemeanor, escalating for repeat offences or video recording",
   "Act must be construed consistently with federal statutes and FAA guidance"
